<rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><language>en</language><title>France 24 - International breaking news, top stories and headlines</title><description>Breaking news and world news from France 24 on Business, Sports, Culture. Video news. News from the US, Europe, Asia Pacific, Africa, Middle East, America</description><link>https://www.france24.com/en/</link><lastBuildDate>Mon, 09 Nov 2026 06:34:46 GMT</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://www.france24.com/en/rss" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><category>Sports</category><title>Marseille defeat RC Lens as they win five in a row in Ligue 1</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/sports/20261109-marseille-defeat-rc-lens-as-they-win-five-in-a-row-in-ligue-1</link><description>
Marseille beat Lens (2-1) in the final game of Ligue 1 matchday 10. Thanks to this result, OM are 4th in the table.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f82883bc-dbe3-11f1-b840-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/om-2.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f82883bc-dbe3-11f1-b840-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/om-2.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">63135774-dbe4-11f1-8c56-f57b33455163</guid><pubDate>Mon, 09 Nov 2026 06:14:33 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>L'Equipe TV</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>Europe to press US on Ukraine peace and Iran at Paris G7 talks</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/france/20261109-europa-us-ukraine-peace-iran-paris-g7-ministers</link><description>
G7 foreign ministers will revisit Russia’s war in Ukraine and the prospect of further US strikes on Iran when they meet in Paris on Monday. Washington has kept the option of new strikes open since Republicans lost the midterm elections. US Secretary of State Marco Rubio is due to attend both days, unlike the March meeting where he only came for one.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/05c2455c-dbe0-11f1-8e22-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26086585080668.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/05c2455c-dbe0-11f1-8e22-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26086585080668.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">65e3357c-dbe0-11f1-9e3d-1df580074fd0</guid><pubDate>Mon, 09 Nov 2026 02:05:00 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/05c2455c-dbe0-11f1-8e22-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26086585080668.jpg">© Michel Euler, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>Trump vows comeback as parties clash over Democrat prosecution threats</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261109-trump-comeback-democrats-prosecution-threats</link><description>
President Donald Trump vowed a political comeback on Sunday after Republicans lost control of Congress in last Tuesday’s midterms, as incoming Democratic leaders pledged to hold his administration to account, and the attorney general promised to defend officials against threatened prosecutions.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/796e5ff4-dafa-11f1-83cc-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/aa618a3631bceeecb3b6ee36d3cb0b937c9f5f89.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/796e5ff4-dafa-11f1-83cc-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/aa618a3631bceeecb3b6ee36d3cb0b937c9f5f89.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">89efa1a6-dbd8-11f1-a76e-03031a2f4c21</guid><pubDate>Mon, 09 Nov 2026 01:13:10 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/796e5ff4-dafa-11f1-83cc-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/aa618a3631bceeecb3b6ee36d3cb0b937c9f5f89.jpg">© Alex Wroblewski, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Technology</category><title>Nvidia to probe reports that Chinese intelligence targeted CEO Jensen Huang</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/technology/20261108-nvidia-jensen-huang-chinese-intelligence-probe</link><description>
Nvidia’s board said Sunday it would investigate reports that CEO Jensen Huang was targeted by a foreign intelligence operation. The New York Times reported Huang had an affair with an executive US intelligence believed was gathering information for Beijing. Huang will remain CEO during the inquiry and has pledged cooperation.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/de28787e-ce09-11f1-932f-8d87bc3aeb3a/w:1024/p:16x9/4be63ee4f4f77ef4291d72acfad4aed31a19b368.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/de28787e-ce09-11f1-932f-8d87bc3aeb3a/w:1024/p:16x9/4be63ee4f4f77ef4291d72acfad4aed31a19b368.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">7cc9fc4e-dbc7-11f1-97ec-dda94e208f61</guid><pubDate>Sun, 08 Nov 2026 23:02:54 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/de28787e-ce09-11f1-932f-8d87bc3aeb3a/w:1024/p:16x9/4be63ee4f4f77ef4291d72acfad4aed31a19b368.jpg">© John Macdougall, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>Pope Leo criticises Milei’s austerity in Argentina, says growth must benefit all</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261108-pope-leo-argentina-visit-milei</link><description>
Pope Leo XIV arrived in Argentina on Sunday from Uruguay, where his Latin America tour began, facing calls to help bridge divisions after three years of austerity under President Javier Milei. The visit to Buenos Aires is the first by a pontiff to the late Pope Francis’s homeland in nearly four decades.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/39bb378c-dbaf-11f1-8a96-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-08T200018Z-1909450093-RC2WJOAQHQ73-RTRMADP-3-POPE-LATAM-ARGENTINA.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/39bb378c-dbaf-11f1-8a96-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-08T200018Z-1909450093-RC2WJOAQHQ73-RTRMADP-3-POPE-LATAM-ARGENTINA.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">4209491c-dbc1-11f1-8d7e-cd9c7bda3277</guid><pubDate>Sun, 08 Nov 2026 22:23:19 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/39bb378c-dbaf-11f1-8a96-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-08T200018Z-1909450093-RC2WJOAQHQ73-RTRMADP-3-POPE-LATAM-ARGENTINA.jpg">© Yara Nardi, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Spotlight</category><title>Pope Leo in Latin America: Papal Politics and Peru</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261108-pope-leo-in-latin-america-papal-politics-and-peru</link><description>
Pope Leo heads to Argentina for the second leg of his South America tour, where he's expected to draw the biggest turnout of his Papacy so far. The pontiff has wrapped up his first visit to Uruguay. Colleen Dulle, Vatican Correspondent at America Magazine and the co-host of the 'Inside the Vatican' podcast, joins us to analyse the significance of his Latin American tour.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/51ec3fd0-dbab-11f1-b6cb-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/ColleenTN811.png"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/51ec3fd0-dbab-11f1-b6cb-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/ColleenTN811.png" type="image/png" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">b628278a-dbb9-11f1-ac32-4364c774d43a</guid><pubDate>Sun, 08 Nov 2026 21:16:48 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Alessandro XENOS</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Israeli opposition leader Eisenkot begins the hard work of forging a coalition government</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261108-israeli-opposition-leader-eisenkot-begins-the-hard-work-of-forging-a-coalition-government</link><description>
Israel's ex-military chief Gadi Eisenkot was tapped by President Isaac Herzog to try to form a government Sunday evening. But his lack of a clear majority in parliament will make trying to forge a coalition alongside the country's divided minor parties an uphill struggle.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/be4c1c22-dbb5-11f1-bbd7-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-08T152158Z-1569314181-RC2RJOASDUSW-RTRMADP-3-ISRAEL-POLITICS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/be4c1c22-dbb5-11f1-bbd7-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-08T152158Z-1569314181-RC2RJOASDUSW-RTRMADP-3-ISRAEL-POLITICS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">369dc2a8-dbb5-11f1-8464-4d6ebdc8c05c</guid><pubDate>Sun, 08 Nov 2026 21:10:13 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/be4c1c22-dbb5-11f1-bbd7-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-08T152158Z-1569314181-RC2RJOASDUSW-RTRMADP-3-ISRAEL-POLITICS.jpg">© Ronen Zvulun, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Pope Leo in Latin America: Papal Politics and Peru</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/pope-leo-in-latin-america-papal-politics-and-peru</link><description>
Pope Leo heads to Argentina for the second leg of his South America tour, where he's expected to draw the biggest turnout of his Papacy so far. The pontiff has wrapped up his first visit to Uruguay. Colleen Dulle, Vatican Correspondent at America Magazine and the co-host of the 'Inside the Vatican' podcast, joins us to analyse the significance of his Latin America trip.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/51ec3fd0-dbab-11f1-b6cb-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/ColleenTN811.png"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/51ec3fd0-dbab-11f1-b6cb-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/ColleenTN811.png" type="image/png" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">4afa2b5c-dbb4-11f1-8c13-1bf2a2dbf315</guid><pubDate>Sun, 08 Nov 2026 20:51:53 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>Migrant boat sinks off Senegal, killing at least 34 people, authorities say</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/africa/20261108-migrant-boat-sinks-off-senegal-killing-at-least-34-people-authorities-say</link><description>
A boat carrying migrants along the hazardous Atlantic Ocean route from West Africa to Europe sank off the coast of Senegal, killed at least 34 people, authorities said Sunday. Only one survivor has so far been found, and "an indeterminate number" are still missing.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8db004c0-db6f-11f1-9c7c-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/c9e8d80cbfc13f8f43d3833c67fbf17f6e5ccb25.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8db004c0-db6f-11f1-9c7c-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/c9e8d80cbfc13f8f43d3833c67fbf17f6e5ccb25.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">2ebc9cba-dbb2-11f1-b6f6-f1ff026c3103</guid><pubDate>Sun, 08 Nov 2026 20:40:33 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8db004c0-db6f-11f1-9c7c-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/c9e8d80cbfc13f8f43d3833c67fbf17f6e5ccb25.jpg">© Patrick Meinhardt, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Ukraine: Russian strikes leave hundreds of thousands without power</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/ukraine-russian-strikes-leave-hundreds-of-thousands-without-power</link><description>
Hundreds of thousands of Ukrainians were left without electricity on Sunday following Russian airstrikes targeting the country's energy infrastructure. Moscow has intensified its attacks as winter approaches, leaving residents in Kyiv and other parts of the country struggling with power cuts as temperatures continue to drop. Clemence Waller reports.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3a894976-db94-11f1-846b-bf1914cabd52/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261108-171056-171236-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3a894976-db94-11f1-846b-bf1914cabd52/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261108-171056-171236-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">3fdd8a5e-db94-11f1-b79f-6343e38d3fa8</guid><pubDate>Sun, 08 Nov 2026 16:59:42 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Gadi Eisenkot receives mandate to form government</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/gadi-eisenkot-receives-mandate-to-form-government</link><description>
Israel's opposition leader Gadi Eisenkot has officially been tasked with forming the country's next government, following a formal announcement by President Isaac Herzog. He now has up to six weeks to negotiate with potential coalition partners and secure a parliamentary majority. While an alliance with Arab Israeli parties appears to be the easiest option mathematically, it remains politically sensitive. Eisenkot must now navigate difficult negotiations to build a coalition capable of replacing Benjamin Netanyahu. Noga Tarnopolsky reports from Jerusalem.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/608ffe0e-db93-11f1-85ef-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261108-160801-161121-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/608ffe0e-db93-11f1-85ef-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261108-160801-161121-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">65b815e2-db93-11f1-9ee7-4943b8d2bb10</guid><pubDate>Sun, 08 Nov 2026 16:58:11 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Sport</category><title>Spain's Alcaraz beats error-prone Shelton to win Paris Masters for first time</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/sport/20261108-spain-s-alcaraz-beats-error-prone-shelton-to-win-paris-masters-for-first-time</link><description>
Spanish tennis star Carlos Alcaraz avenged his loss to American player Ben Shelton in the US Open in September as he inched ahead of his rival Sunday to win the Paris Masters for the first time. It was Shelton's first defeat in a Masters final.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e7a1efda-db91-11f1-95fc-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/f75fa6fa8ded7fbfacd31db319351a05d3ba1ad3.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e7a1efda-db91-11f1-95fc-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/f75fa6fa8ded7fbfacd31db319351a05d3ba1ad3.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">e86e877a-db91-11f1-b8e6-9355be3483f4</guid><pubDate>Sun, 08 Nov 2026 16:31:53 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e7a1efda-db91-11f1-95fc-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/f75fa6fa8ded7fbfacd31db319351a05d3ba1ad3.jpg">© Dimitar Dilkoff, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>The week in pictures: US midterms 'Blue Wave', French protests and Dakar Youth Olympics</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261108-the-week-in-pictures-trump-midterms-debacle-french-protests-dakar-youth-olympics</link><description>
From the Democratic Party's big wins in the US midterm elections to France's ongoing student-led protests and the first Olympic sports event held on African soil, FRANCE 24 looks back at some of the week's most striking images.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/32d96078-db74-11f1-b6c9-bf1914cabd52/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26310471490191.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/32d96078-db74-11f1-b6c9-bf1914cabd52/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26310471490191.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">b6cb3870-db7e-11f1-a1cc-330d38f8a0f8</guid><pubDate>Sun, 08 Nov 2026 16:21:34 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/32d96078-db74-11f1-b6c9-bf1914cabd52/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26310471490191.jpg">© Kieran Cleeves, OIS/IOC via AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Tech 24</category><title>US voters reject AI data centres: could the backlash spread to France?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/tech-24/20261108-us-voters-reject-ai-data-centres-could-the-backlash-spread-to-france</link><description>
In Tuesday’s US midterm elections, voters weighed in on more than 40 local measures on data centres, and sided against them in all but one. With Democrats taking control of Congress in January and new governors in Texas and Georgia calling for moratoriums, the AI building boom faces its toughest political test yet.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4636e71a-db80-11f1-a6d8-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-WB-TECH24-MIDTERMS-DATA-CENTRE-FALLOUT.png"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4636e71a-db80-11f1-a6d8-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-WB-TECH24-MIDTERMS-DATA-CENTRE-FALLOUT.png" type="image/png" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">c73f8e88-db81-11f1-8ff5-dbf7c48ee3c6</guid><pubDate>Sun, 08 Nov 2026 14:36:25 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Peter O'BRIEN</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Yemen's humanitarian crisis worsens</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/yemen-s-humanitarian-crisis-worsens</link><description>
One month into the Yemeni government's offensive against the Iran-aligned Houthis, fighting continues to escalate along the Red Sea coast. Meanwhile, the humanitarian crisis is worsening, with hundreds of thousands of people displaced and the country facing the threat of catastrophe. Rula Amin, Senior Communications Advisor and spokesperson at UNHCR at Amman, in Jordan, shares further details.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/61e95800-db7e-11f1-961e-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261108-140416-140658-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/61e95800-db7e-11f1-961e-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261108-140416-140658-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">6735dcac-db7e-11f1-b6b0-a3bc1c7deeec</guid><pubDate>Sun, 08 Nov 2026 14:22:14 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Poland in shock after 6 killed in Krakow far-right shooting</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/poland-in-shock-after-6-killed-in-krakow-far-right-shooting</link><description>
Poland on Sunday launched a terror probe into the mass shooting in Krakow the day before, in which six people were killed and many more were injured. Authorities have said that the 24-year-old suspect, who used a semi-automatic rifle in his killing spree, was “fascinated by far-right ideologies”. He is currently in critical condition in hospital. FRANCE 24 journalist Adrien Sariat reports from Poland.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/5cea55f2-db7e-11f1-bd0a-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261108-150134-150232-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/5cea55f2-db7e-11f1-bd0a-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261108-150134-150232-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">620ad868-db7e-11f1-9f57-c1ea51b6f7a3</guid><pubDate>Sun, 08 Nov 2026 14:21:18 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>French skipper wins Route du Rhum</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/french-skipper-wins-route-du-rhum</link><description>
French sailor Tom Laperche has won the Route du Rhum, setting a new record in the transatlantic yacht race. The 29-year-old crossed the finish line in Guadeloupe on his first attempt, beating the previous 2022 record by around six hours. A remarkable debut in one of sailing's toughest competitions!
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/83ffbb5a-db7e-11f1-adef-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261108-150723-150909-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/83ffbb5a-db7e-11f1-adef-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261108-150723-150909-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">8908bf7a-db7e-11f1-a60f-8bcd096c4ca7</guid><pubDate>Sun, 08 Nov 2026 14:20:04 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Mourning in Poland after mass shooting</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/mourning-in-poland-after-mass-shooting</link><description>
Poland has launched a terrorism investigation after a deadly shooting left six people dead and 16 injured. The 24-year-old Polish suspect was reportedly fascinated by far-right ideologies. Authorities are investigating the possible extremist motive as Krakow's main square remains sealed. Two days of national mourning have been declared for the victims.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ac245178-db7d-11f1-9478-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261108-140118-140318-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ac245178-db7d-11f1-9478-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261108-140118-140318-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">b127f486-db7d-11f1-8be9-85907240b2be</guid><pubDate>Sun, 08 Nov 2026 14:18:48 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Europe will take part in US-mediated Ukraine talks in Abu Dhabi, French FM says</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261108-europe-will-take-part-us-mediated-ukraine-peace-talks-abu-dhabi-french-fm-says</link><description>
France will participate in the upcoming Abu Dhabi peace talks on ending the Ukraine war, Foreign Minister Jean-Noël Barrot said Sunday, adding that Europeans will be represented at the summit. The talks will take place under US mediation on Tuesday and Wednesday.
